    "enable": {
      "word": "ENABLE",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "To give strength or ability to; to make firm and strong. [Obs.] \"Who hath enabled me.\" 1 Tim. i. 12. Receive the Holy Ghost, said Christ to his apostles, when he enabled them with priestly power. Jer. Taylor.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To make able (to do, or to be, something); to confer sufficient power upon; to furnish with means, opportunities, and the like; to render competent for; to empower; to endow. Temperance gives Nature her full play, and enables her to exert herself in all her force and vigor. Addison.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        }
      ],
